<title>FRANCE: France's INSEE details 1997 economic forecasts.</title>
<headline>France's INSEE details 1997 economic forecasts.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a breakdown of 1997 forecasts for the French economy, issued by national statistics institute INSEE.</p>
<p>GROSS DOMESTIC PRODUCT (VOLUME) BY TYPE OF EXPENDITURE Percent</p>
<p>change from previous period</p>
<p>				 1997</p>
<p>				 Q1   Q2   Q3   Q4  1995 1996 1997</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> GDP (100 %)		 0.2  1.2  0.7  1.0  2.1  1.5  2.3</p>
<p> Imports (29%)	    -0.6  2.2  1.9  2.0  5.1  2.6  4.4</p>
<p> (of which merchandise) -0.6  2.2  1.9  2.0  5.8  2.3  4.5</p>
<p> Household cons (60%)    0.4  0.4  0.7  0.7  1.7  2.1  1.0</p>
<p> General govt cons(19%)  0.2  0.3  0.5  0.4  0.0  1.2  1.3</p>
<p> Total investment(20%)  -1.3  1.3  0.8  1.0  2.5 -0.5  0.8</p>
<p>  Corporate sector(11%) -1.4  2.3  0.6  1.2  3.3 -0.7  1.6</p>
<p>  Households(5%)	  -2.8  0.2  1.6  0.9  2.3 -0.2 -0.6</p>
<p>  Other sectors(4%)	0.8 -0.1  0.1  0.3  0.4 -0.3  0.0</p>
<p> Exports(29%)		1.1  2.2  2.0  1.9  6.3  4.8  7.0</p>
<p> (of which merchandise)  1.5  2.2  1.9  1.9  7.9  5.1  7.4</p>
<p> Domestic demand	  -0.3  1.2  0.7  1.0  1.8  0.9  1.4</p>
<p>-----------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>CONTRIBUTIONS TO THE GROWTH OF GDP</p>
<p> Inventory changes	-0.3  0.6  0.0  0.3  0.3 -0.5  0.4</p>
<p> Trade in goods&amp;services 0.5  0.1  0.0  0.0  0.3  0.6  0.8</p>
<p> Domestic demand excl.</p>
<p> inventories		 0.0  0.6  0.7  0.7  1.5  1.4  1.0</p>
<p>-----------------------------------------------------------</p>
